# registry-triage.prl — the visible list of parser constructs that the
# published specification (Annex A) does not yet register (kernel rule
# R1; 01-audit.md D1; 09-migration-plan.md phase 0). The
# registry-parity test (test/registry-parity.test.ts) fails for any
# parser keyword that is neither in Annex A nor marked here, and fails
# for any entry that has since gained a specification section — the
# list only shrinks, and the construction freeze (phase 0) means
# nothing joins the parser while entries are open.
#
# Dispositions follow the triage of 09-migration-plan.md phase 2 and
# the layering of 08-oiml-extensions.md: specify-as-platform-module
# (layer 2), specify-as-oiml-extension (layer 3), merge (into the
# surviving process dialect), or a bare unspecified-pending-triage
# where the triage decision is not yet recorded.

promise_set unspecified-pending-triage (specify as a platform module — file 08, the promise register of the certificate lineage)
